@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run with Node.js 22 or later:
+
+```sh
+npm start
+npm test
+npm run audit:privacy
+```
+
+`PORT` defaults to 11222. There are no runtime or build dependencies. The previous start command downloaded an unpinned static server; the new server uses only Node built-ins and serves an explicit allowlist. Deploy using this server: a generic static host will not automatically apply its headers.
+
+## Privacy and third-party audit
+
+Reviewed October 16, 2026. Scope: all shipped HTML, CSS, assets, package dependencies, and HTTP routes. This is a source and automated HTTP audit, not an independent vendor certification or a browser network audit.
+
+| Component | Finding / control |
+| --- | --- |
+| Hero image | Previously loaded from images.unsplash.com on every visit, exposing connection metadata. Downloaded once and served locally at `/assets/coffee.jpg`. Source: https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1350&q=80 |
+| Fonts, scripts, embeds, analytics | None. System fonts and local styles only. CSP blocks scripts, connections, forms, and third-party resources. |
+| Application data | No forms, accounts, sessions, payments, database, cookies, browser storage, or profiling. Existing menu, ordering, and account links are unimplemented placeholders. |
+| Request handling | Connection metadata exists only during requests; no application access logs, request reflection, or persistence. Unknown files return a generic 404. Writes return 405. |
+| Browser state | No cookies are set. `/logout` clears legacy cookies, storage, and caches with Clear-Site-Data; secure contexts and browser support are required. There is no server session to invalidate. |
+| Dependencies | Zero third-party production/development packages. Maintain and patch the Node runtime. |
+| Hosting/CDN | Not present in this repository; operator must review providers and configure their logs and retention before launch. |
+
+Repeat the audit on every integration/dependency change and quarterly. `npm run audit:privacy` checks shipped sources for external URLs, executable/inline content and data collection, and exercises the real HTTP server for headers, MIME types, route isolation, method handling, cross-site requests, and logout. Review new network-capable code and CSS manually in code review; static patterns are a regression guard, not a complete network audit.
+
+## Deployment and secure handling
+
+- Terminate TLS at a trusted reverse proxy, redirect public HTTP to HTTPS there, and keep the Node port private. Set `NODE_ENV=production` for HSTS. It starts at 300 seconds to permit a safe rollout; raise to one year after verifying HTTPS. Subdomain and preload commitments are intentionally excluded.
+- Ensure proxies/CDNs preserve response headers, honor `no-store` and `Vary`, and do not inject scripts or externally hosted assets. Do not log request URLs, query strings, IP addresses, cookies, authorization headers, or request bodies. Disable provider access logging where possible; document a specific purpose and short retention for any required security logs.
+- CSP blocks all scripts because this application requires none; styles were extracted to avoid `unsafe-inline`. Browser violation reporting is deliberately disabled: there is no established need to collect visitors' document URLs or script samples. Failures remain visible in browser consoles; automated checks cover known routes. No SharedArrayBuffer requirement exists, so COEP is unnecessary.
+- No sensitive endpoints or stored records exist to encrypt, rate-limit, export, or delete. Do not introduce speculative data collection. Before implementing orders/accounts, define each field's purpose, minimum granularity, retention and automatic deletion, server-side authorization, validation, rate limits, encryption and secret management, and access/correction/export/deletion flows. Offer guest ordering. Session cookies must use `__Host-`, `Secure`, `HttpOnly`, `SameSite=Lax`, `Path=/`, and no Domain; invalidate server sessions on logout.
+- Review any future vendor's data flow, purpose, retention, subprocessors, and deletion controls before integration. Obtain appropriate consent before optional collection and update the privacy notice. Keep embeds behind explicit user activation and local previews. Never place tokens or personal information in URLs, browser storage, or logs.
