+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html lang="en">
+<head>
+  <meta charset="UTF-8">
+  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
+  <meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer">
+  <title>Privacy | The Daily Grind</title>
+  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css">
+</head>
+<body>
+  <nav aria-label="Main"><a class="logo" href="/">THE DAILY GRIND</a><a href="/">Back to home</a></nav>
+  <main class="container policy">
+    <h1>Your privacy, by default</h1>
+    <p>Last updated: October 16, 2026</p>
+    <p>You can browse this website without creating an account or sharing personal details.</p>
+    <h2>What we collect</h2>
+    <p>This application has no data collection forms, analytics, advertising, fingerprinting, or user database. It does not set cookies or store information in your browser.</p>
+    <p>To deliver pages, our server necessarily receives connection information such as your IP address, the requested URL, and browser headers. The application does not log or retain this information after the request.</p>
+    <h2>No third-party tracking</h2>
+    <p>Images and styles are served from this website. Browsing does not load third-party scripts, fonts, embeds, or images. We do not sell personal information or use it for marketing.</p>
+    <h2>Your data and choices</h2>
+    <p>There is no application profile to access, correct, export, or delete. The account, rewards, and ordering links are placeholders; they do not currently collect data or process orders. You do not need to accept tracking to browse.</p>
+    <h2>Hosting and security</h2>
+    <p>Security policies limit what this website can load and which device features it can access. Hosting and network providers may process connection information under their own policies. Their logging and retention settings must be reviewed by the site operator before deployment.</p>
+    <h2>Future changes</h2>
+    <p>If we introduce orders, accounts, or other services that need personal details, we will explain the purpose and retention period before collecting them and provide ways to manage that data.</p>
+    <p><a class="btn" href="/">Back to your daily grind</a></p>
+  </main>
+  <footer><p>&copy; 2026 The Daily Grind Coffee Co.</p></footer>
+</body>
+</html>
